<p>Two kinds of helper live here. <strong>Ghost's</strong> are modelled by <code>site/lib/ghost.mjs</code> so every partial renders in the docs exactly as it will in a theme; <strong>the docs' own</strong> exist only on this site. The utilities are Tailwind <code>@utility</code> rules, so they take variants (<code>md:im-stack</code>).</p>

<h2>Customising in depth</h2>
<p>The pages under Collections and Pages are <strong>compositions, not templates to copy whole</strong>: every one is components plus a few layout classes, and everything they are made of reads a token. So there are three levels to change a page at, and the right one is the lowest that does the job:</p>
<ol>
<li><strong>A token</strong> — <code>--im-accent</code>, <code>--im-radius-xl</code>, <code>--im-width-page</code>. Changes every component that uses it, in both themes. See Foundation.</li>
<li><strong>A knob</strong> — a component's own custom property, like <code>--im-player-side</code> or <code>--im-navpanel-width</code>. Set it on the component, a wrapper, or <code>:root</code>; every one is listed below with its default.</li>
<li><strong>A helper</strong> — a utility on one element, for one instance: <code>md:grid-cols-3</code>, <code>gap-6</code>, <code>text-muted</code>, <code>rounded-2xl</code>. Utilities sit in the last layer, so they beat any component rule without <code>!important</code>.</li>
</ol>

<h2>Helpers that always ship</h2>
<p>Tailwind only writes the utilities it finds, and a theme that vendors <code>im.css</code> does not run Tailwind — so <code>src/utilities/helpers.css</code> guarantees a fixed set is in the bundle whatever the docs use. They are Tailwind's own names, unprefixed, and each one reads a token: <code>p-4</code> is 4 × <code>--im-space</code>, <code>bg-surface</code> is <code>--im-surface</code>. Nothing here names a hue: <code>bg-red-500</code> does not exist.</p>
