<p>Need one that is not on the list? A theme that runs Tailwind itself can use any utility against the same bridge (<code>src/foundation/tokens/tailwind.css</code>); a theme that only vendors <code>im.css</code> adds a line to <code>helpers.css</code> and rebuilds. To change a component everywhere, set its knob rather than repeating utilities on every instance.</p>

<h2>Knobs, component by component</h2>
<p>Every custom property a component exposes, read from its stylesheet at build time — declared on its own selector, or read with a fallback so it only exists when you set it (the default then shows as the fallback). Set a knob on the component itself for one instance, on a wrapper for a region, or on <code>:root</code> for the whole site.</p>
